\DOC WORD_FORALL_OFFSET_TAC

\TYPE {WORD_FORALL_OFFSET_TAC : int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Rewrites a universally quantified goal so that a quantified pointer variable is
shifted by a fixed offset: occurrences of the variable minus the offset become
the bare variable, and bare occurrences gain the offset.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {n : int} is the byte offset by which the quantified pointer is
shifted; it may be supplied as a literal or as a bound integer expression. The
goal must have a universally quantified word-valued variable occurring in the
body both bare and offset downwards by {n}. The conclusion {t} is re-expressed
relative to the shifted pointer: downward-offset occurrences become bare, bare
occurrences become offset upwards by {n}, and further additive offsets
accumulate accordingly.
{
      A ?- !x1 ... xn. t
      ==================  WORD_FORALL_OFFSET_TAC n
      A ?- !x1 ... xn. u
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of transformation, applied to goals
whose conclusion is a universally quantified implication about a machine-level
specification.

\ENDDOC
